OL,3,AWhy Australia chose the world's biggest
OL,4,Apolitical stage to reveal OpenAI hack
OL,5,
OL,6,FAustralia made a dramatic revelation on
OL,7,FWednesday during the United Nations
OL,8,FGeneral Assembly.
OL,10,FRogue AI agents had hacked one of its
OL,11,Fgovernment bodies - the first known
OL,12,Fincident of its kind in the world.
OL,13,FPrivate data, but not sensitive
OL,14,Finformation, was taken from Medicare,
OL,15,FAustralia's universal healthcare
OL,16,Fscheme.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,109,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11908
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790342334
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AWhy Australia chose the world's biggest
OL,4,Apolitical stage to reveal OpenAI hack
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe breach happened in June, but OpenAI
OL,7,Fsays it only became aware of it in
OL,8,FAugust - and then took until 10
OL,9,FSeptember to alert Australia's
OL,10,Fgovernment, by sending an email to an
OL,11,Faddress used by researchers and
OL,12,Facademics to alert authorities to
OL,13,Fconcerns of vulnerabilities.
OL,15,FWhile worrying, the timing of the
OL,16,Fincident is somewhat of a gift for
OL,17,FAustralia.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG8/19
